--
-- Description
-- -----------
-- This tests that the overflow detection of the RX path is working correctly
-- in DMA mode.
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
-- -------------------
-- � Checks operation of overflow detection in the RX FIFO
-- � Checks operation of the pipeline overflow detection in gem_rx.
-- � Checks operation of the rx overflow interrupt
-- � Checks the discarding of frames by the DMA when an overflow occurs
--
-- Detailed Test Description
-- -------------------------
-- 1. Setup the wait states to ensure that the overflow operation can be tested.
-- 2. Initialise the GEM for gigabit receive operation into a 32 bit DMA bus.
-- 3. Enable all interrupts.
-- 4. Receive a minimum length frame. Gigabit operation into a 32 bit DMA bus
--    with wait states, will result in an rx overflow of the FIFO.
--    Check that this causes the frame to be dropped and verify that the buffer 
--    is correctly recovered for the next frame.
--    Also check that an rx overrun interrupt is raised, a receive overrun 
--    status is reported in receive status register and that the receive 
--    overrun statistics register is incremented.
-- 5. Switch to 100M mode at 32-bit DMA bus width.
-- 6. Receive two frames at minimum IFG. The first frame should be of minimum
--    length, the second frame should be very short so that it comes out of 
--    the pipeline (pipeline_finished) whilst the status update to the DMA and
--    registers block is still in progress (update_in_progress still active).
--    Check that the first frame is received correctly, but the second frame is
--    dropped silently (runt frame).
--    Note due to new fix, a runt will not cause an overflow in this situation.
-- 7. Switch to gigabit, full duplex, PCS mode at 64-bit DMA bus width.
-- 8. Receive two frames at minimum IFG. The first frame should be of minimum
--    length, the second frame should be very short so that the end of frame is
--    written into the pipeline before the previous end of frame has come out 
--    of the pipeline. 
--    Check that the first frame is received correctly, but the second frame is
--    dropped silently (runt frame).
--    Note due to new fix, a runt will not cause an overflow in this situation.
-- 9. Receive two frames at minimum IFG. The first frame should be too long
--    (> 1518 bytes) and the second frame should be very short so that it 
--    comes out of the pipeline (pipeline_finished) whilst the status update to
--    the DMA and registers block is still in progress (update_in_progress still
--    active).
--    Check that the first frame is  received correctly, but the second frame is
--    dropped and that this generates a receive overrun interrupt, status 
--    and statistic.
--10. Switch to gigabit mode at 64-bit DMA bus width.
--11. Receive a good frame and check that the DMA receive buffer is correctly
--    recovered, and that a good status is recorded.
--12. Check the status and statistics registers and ensure that the above 
--    operations were handled properly.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------


--******************************************************************************
-- 1. Setup the wait states to ensure that the overflow operation can be tested.
--******************************************************************************
wait_states 6
bus_grant_delay 6


--******************************************************************************
-- 2. Initialise the GEM for gigabit receive operation into a 32 bit DMA bus.
-- 3. Enable all interrupts.
--******************************************************************************

apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbwr      18 01234008  -- write receive queue pointer
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      98 12345678  -- specific address register 1 bottom
apbwr      9C 00001111  -- specific address register 1 top
apbwr      04 00080400  -- setup for gigabit operation in 32 bit mode
apbwr      00 00000004  -- enable receive
apbrd      20 00000000  -- check contents of the receive status register 



--******************************************************************************
-- 7. Switch to gigabit, full duplex, PCS mode at 64-bit DMA bus width.
--******************************************************************************

apbrd     200 00009040  -- check value of pcs control register
apbwr     200 00000040  -- disable autonegotioation
apbrd     200 00008040  -- check autoneg disabled
apbwr      04 00280c02  -- Setup PCS mode and 64 bits and full duplex
apbrd      04 00280c02  -- verify write

-- check for link status change
apbrd(int) 24 00000200  -- check interrupt status - link status change

dma_rd 01234008 44444000 -- reads locations of next rx buffer



--******************************************************************************
-- 8. Receive two frames at minimum IFG. The first frame should be of minimum
--    length, the second frame should be very short so that the end of frame is
--    written into the pipeline before the previous end of frame has come out 
--    of the pipeline. 
--    Check that the first frame is received correctly, but the second frame is
--    dropped silently (runt frame).
--    Note due to new fix, a runt will not cause an overflow in this situation.
--******************************************************************************

apbrd      20 00000000  "Scenario 3: RX pipeline EOF overflow"
                        -- check contents of the receive status register 

-- buffer will be recovered so no descriptor read

-- -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- trigger reception of next receive frame at time interval after TBI is enabled
pcs_rxd(1002)   5555d578563412111111112222222233333333
pcs_rxd               44444444555555556666666677777777
pcs_rxd               8888888899999999aaaaaaaabbbbbbbb
pcs_rxd               000000000000000000000000gggggggg

-- drive in receive frame for second frame (just preamble, SFD, 9 bytes & CRC)
pcs_rxd(gap) 5555d5785634121111111122
pcs_rxd            gggggggg

-- begin to store 1st frame to memory
dma_wr 44444000 12345678
dma_wr 44444004 11111111
dma_wr 44444008 22222222
dma_wr 4444400c 33333333
dma_wr 44444010 44444444
dma_wr 44444014 55555555
dma_wr 44444018 66666666
dma_wr 4444401c 77777777
dma_wr 44444020 88888888
dma_wr 44444024 99999999
dma_wr 44444028 aaaaaaaa
dma_wr 4444402c bbbbbbbb
dma_wr 44444030 00000000
dma_wr 44444034 00000000
dma_wr 44444038 00000000
dma_wr 4444403c 9b303826

dma_wr 0123400c 0c00c040 -- dma writes rx status, address match 3 & 64 bytes
dma_wr 01234008 44444001 -- dma writes ownership bit

dma_rd 01234010 55555000 -- reads locations of next rx buffer


-- NEW FIX MEANS RUNT PACKET IS DROPPED SILENTLY WITH NO OVERFLOW

apbrd(int) 24 00000002  "Scenario 3: Complete"
                        -- check interrupt status - Receive OK
apbrd      20 00000002  -- check receive status register - Receive OK
apbwr      20 00000002  -- clear Receive overrun
apbrd     1A4 00000000  -- check receive overrun statistic
-- -----------------------------------------------------------------------------



--******************************************************************************
-- 9. Receive two frames at minimum IFG. The first frame should be too long
--    (> 1518 bytes) and the second frame should be very short so that it 
--    comes out of the pipeline (pipeline_finished) whilst the status update to
--    the DMA and registers block is still in progress (update_in_progress still
--    active).
--    Check that the first frame is  received correctly, but the second frame is
--    dropped and that this generates a receive overrun interrupt, status 
--    and statistic.
--******************************************************************************
-- This is currently not possible given pipeline depth of 10 and length of time
-- taken to update register block (clock ratios used)

apbrd      20 00000000  "Scenario 4: RX status update overflow (too long)"
apbrd      24 00000000  "Scenario 4: Complete"



--******************************************************************************
--10. Switch to gigabit mode at 64-bit DMA bus width.
--******************************************************************************

apbwr      04 00280400  -- Setup gigabit mode and 64 bits
apbrd      04 00280400  -- verify write

-- check for link status change
apbrd(int) 24 00000200  -- check interrupt status - link status change



--******************************************************************************
--11. Receive a good frame and check that the DMA receive buffer is correctly
--    recovered, and that a good status is recorded.
--******************************************************************************

apbrdf     20 00000000  "Scenario 5: RX good frame"
                        -- check contents of the receive status register 
                        -- and trigger reception of frame

-- drive in receive frame
rxd(apb_x)   55d578563412111111112222222233333333
rxd              44444444555555556666666677777777
rxd              8888888899999999aaaaaaaabbbbbbbb
rxd              0000000000000000000000002638309b

-- store frame to memory
dma_wr 55555000 12345678
dma_wr 55555004 11111111
dma_wr 55555008 22222222
dma_wr 5555500c 33333333
dma_wr 55555010 44444444
dma_wr 55555014 55555555
dma_wr 55555018 66666666
dma_wr 5555501c 77777777
dma_wr 55555020 88888888
dma_wr 55555024 99999999
dma_wr 55555028 aaaaaaaa
dma_wr 5555502c bbbbbbbb
dma_wr 55555030 00000000
dma_wr 55555034 00000000
dma_wr 55555038 00000000
dma_wr 5555503c 9b303826

dma_wr 01234014 0c00c040 -- dma writes rx status, address match 3 & 64 bytes
dma_wr 01234010 55555001 -- dma writes ownership bit

dma_rd 01234018 66666000 -- reads locations of next rx buffer

-- frame successfully stored
apbrd(int) 24 00000002  "Scenario 5: Complete"
                        -- check interrupt status - Receive complete
apbrd      20 00000002  -- check receive status register - Receive complete
apbwr      20 00000002  -- clear Receive complete



--******************************************************************************
--12. Check the status and statistics registers and ensure that the above 
--    operations were handled properly.
--******************************************************************************

-- check transmit statistics
apbrd     100 00000000  -- check octets transmitted bottom
apbrd     104 00000000  -- check octets transmitted top
apbrd     108 00000000  -- check frames transmitted ok
apbrd     10C 00000000  -- check broadcast frames transmitted
apbrd     110 00000000  -- check multicast frames transmitted
apbrd     114 00000000  -- check pause frames transmitted
apbrd     118 00000000  -- check frames transmitted 64
apbrd     11C 00000000  -- check frames transmitted 65-127
apbrd     120 00000000  -- check frames transmitted 128-255
apbrd     124 00000000  -- check frames transmitted 256-511
apbrd     128 00000000  -- check frames transmitted 512-1023
apbrd     12C 00000000  -- check frames transmitted 1024-1518
apbrd     130 00000000  -- check frames transmitted 1519
apbrd     134 00000000  -- check transmit underruns errors
apbrd     138 00000000  -- check single collisions frames
apbrd     13C 00000000  -- check multiple collisions frames
apbrd     140 00000000  -- check excessive collisions frames
apbrd     144 00000000  -- check late collisions frames
apbrd     148 00000000  -- check deferred frames
apbrd     14C 00000000  -- check carrier sense errors

-- check receive statistics
apbrd     150 00000080  -- check octets received bottom
apbrd     154 00000000  -- check octets received top
apbrd     158 00000002  -- check frames received ok
apbrd     15C 00000000  -- check broadcast frames received
apbrd     160 00000000  -- check multicast frames received
apbrd     164 00000000  -- check pause frames received
apbrd     168 00000002  -- check frames received 64
apbrd     16C 00000000  -- check frames received 65-127
apbrd     170 00000000  -- check frames received 128-255
apbrd     174 00000000  -- check frames received 256-511
apbrd     178 00000000  -- check frames received 512-1023
apbrd     17C 00000000  -- check frames received 1024-1518
apbrd     180 00000000  -- check frames received 1519
apbrd     184 00000000  -- check undersize frame errors
apbrd     188 00000000  -- check excessive receive length errors
apbrd     18C 00000000  -- check receive jabbers errors
apbrd     190 00000000  -- check FCS errors
apbrd     194 00000000  -- check receive length errors
apbrd     198 00000000  -- check receive symbol errors
apbrd     19C 00000000  -- check alignment errors
apbrd     1A0 00000000  -- check receive resource errors
apbrd     1A4 00000000  -- check receive overrun errors


-- force end of test in case it doesn't stop of its own accord
end(2000)

